# ===========================================
# ✅ WHAT TO COMMIT (Exceptions)
# ===========================================
# DO commit:
# - .env.example (template with placeholder values)
# - requirements.txt (dependencies)
# - package.json, package-lock.json (frontend dependencies)
# - Dockerfile (container definitions)
# - docker-compose.yml (orchestration)
# - *.tf (Terraform configurations, NOT state)
# - *.yaml, *.yml (Kubernetes manifests, NOT secrets)
# - README.md, docs/ (documentation)
# - tests/ (test code)
# - src/, app/ (source code)
# - infrastructure/ (IaC configs, NOT state)

# ===========================================
# 🔒 SECURITY NOTES
# ===========================================
# 1. NEVER commit .env files with real credentials
# 2. Rotate any secrets accidentally committed
# 3. Use secret management tools (AWS Secrets Manager, HashiCorp Vault)
# 4. Enable secret scanning in GitHub/GitLab
# 5. Use pre-commit hooks to prevent secret commits (see .pre-commit-config.yaml)

# ===========================================
# 🎯 PRE-COMMIT HOOKS
# ===========================================
# Install pre-commit to prevent accidental commits:
# pip install pre-commit
# pre-commit install
#
# See .pre-commit-config.yaml for configuration

# ===========================================
# END OF .gitignore
# ===========================================
